note The GUI scenarios: the document's toggles, the peek and tooltip, the listing and pin selection, the graph's expansions, drag and zoom, the side panels, search and the command line, deletions, the diff tab and live reload. Each settles with idle and a save first: with several servers missing, the status line otherwise says whichever failure came last. SETTLE then opens startup by clicking paths/2, since the paths list reads c-lib, shapes, startup, stats. A Scenario is its setup (Missing when a tool is not on PATH), the script, a hook that sees every stderr line with a rect <marker> line in the script as its cue, and after, CLI commands run once the GUI quits with their output appended to the golden gui-<fn>.

