note Plays a GUI scenario. A script line aiming at <<prefix>> is resolved first by a probe run of the script up to that line, on a fresh fixture, reading the rectangle the probe's dump or rect printed; the final run then starts from the same state. <<prefix>> stands for the centre of the last stderr line starting with prefix, <<prefix|dx,dy>> for a point offset from its top-left corner. Offsets are pixels: the scripts assume the fixed 1600x1000 script window at scale 1, 16 px rows. The screenshots land in shots(name).

